    reviewCount: 6200,
    pros: [
      "Three-stage design (sediment, catalytic carbon, sub-micron post-filter) handles chlorine, chloramine, VOCs, and particulate down to 5 microns",
      "1.25-inch model flows 12 to 20 GPM, so pressure barely dips when multiple fixtures run at once",
      "NSF/ANSI 42 rated media for chlorine taste and odor reduction",
      "Roughly one million gallons or 6 years of filter life before the main media needs replacing",
      "Digital control head automates backwashing — no manual cartridge swaps",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Upfront cost is steep — unit plus professional install commonly lands north of $1,800 to $2,200",
      "Backwash cycling uses extra water and needs a nearby floor drain",
