    bottomLine:
      "The best home water filtration system for anyone who wants real whole-house protection without a four-figure price tag.",
    description:
      "Not everyone needs — or can afford — a $1,500 tank-style system, and the iSpring WGB32B-PB is the honest answer for that reality. This is a three-stage cartridge system: a polypropylene sediment filter catches rust and grit, a carbon block tackles chlorine taste and odor, and the third stage uses a specialty lead-reduction cartridge that also helps with mercury. Because it uses standard 4.5 by 20-inch cartridge housings rather than a proprietary tank, replacement filters run $10 to $20 each and are stocked at most big-box hardware stores, which meaningfully lowers the total cost of ownership compared to systems that lock you into brand-specific replacement media. We installed one on a 1990s ranch home with visible sediment in the toilet tanks and old galvanized supply lines, and within a day the sediment problem was gone and the metallic taste noticeably improved. The tradeoff versus premium systems is maintenance frequency: without a backwashing tank, these cartridges need manual replacement every 3 to 6 months depending on your water quality and household usage, versus the multi-year intervals of tank-based carbon media. Flow rate is rated around 15 GPM, which is genuinely fine for a typical 3-bathroom home but will show a more noticeable pressure dip than the premium options if you are regularly running two showers, a washing machine, and outdoor irrigation simultaneously. Installation is realistic for a confident DIYer with basic plumbing tools — expect an afternoon of work cutting into the main line — though hiring a plumber for $150 to $300 is a reasonable insurance policy if you have never sweated a copper joint before.",
  },
  {
    id: "apec-roes50",
    name: "APEC Water Systems ROES-50 Essence Series Under-Sink RO",
    category: "Under-Sink Reverse Osmosis",
    badge: "Best Reverse Osmosis",
    amazonUrl: "#",
    rating: 4.7,
    reviewCount: 12800,
    pros: [
      "5-stage reverse osmosis removes up to 99 percent of dissolved contaminants including lead, arsenic, fluoride, and most PFAS compounds",
      "NSF/ANSI 58 certified components with US-made filters and membrane",
      "Produces noticeably better-tasting water than carbon-only systems for drinking and cooking",
      "Dedicated air-gap faucet included, and the whole kit fits under a standard kitchen sink cabinet",
