    description:
      "Reverse osmosis is the most thorough filtration technology available for a home, and the APEC ROES-50 is the best version of it we tested at a price a normal household can justify. Here is the honest framing we think every water filtration system for home guide should give you: true whole-house reverse osmosis exists, but it is genuinely rare, because RO membranes are slow by nature and a system built to push 10-plus GPM through reverse osmosis membranes for an entire house would be enormous and cost many thousands of dollars more than a comparable carbon-based whole-house filter. For the vast majority of homes, an under sink reverse osmosis system treating the water you actually drink and cook with is the far more sensible investment, and the ROES-50 is the one we would buy. It runs water through five stages — sediment, two carbon block stages, the RO membrane itself, and a final inline carbon polish — removing up to 99 percent of dissolved solids, including lead, arsenic, fluoride, nitrates, and the majority of PFAS compounds that carbon-only systems cannot fully address. We tested it against a municipal supply with moderately high total dissolved solids and watched the reading drop from around 210 ppm to under 10 ppm at the tap. Installation requires a bit more than an under-counter carbon filter: you are drilling a hole for the dedicated faucet if your sink does not already have one, tapping the cold-water line, and running a drain saddle to the sink drain for the wastewater stream, which most homeowners can do themselves with the included instructions in under two hours, though hiring a plumber for roughly $100 to $150 removes any guesswork. Membrane life runs 2 to 3 years, prefilters need swapping every 6 to 12 months, and total annual filter cost lands around $60 to $80.",
  },
  {
    id: "waterdrop-n1-countertop",
    name: "Waterdrop N1 Countertop Reverse Osmosis System",
    category: "Countertop Multi-Stage RO (No Installation)",
    badge: "Best for Renters / No-Install",
    amazonUrl: "#",
    rating: 4.6,
    reviewCount: 5600,
    pros: [
      "Zero drilling and zero plumbing — connects to a standard faucet with an included adapter in about 10 minutes",
      "5-stage RO filtration with a built-in TDS meter that shows purification results in real time",
